              {
                "end": 719,
                "rank": 1,
                "text": "# Harbor archive: Night Restore R-17 acceptance rule\nDocument status: approved. Scope: Night Restore R-17 only.\nThis is an invented archive and invented equipment in a synthetic local evaluation. Nothing here is a public-source fact, operational incident, or production benchmark.\nR-17 acceptance requires BOTH: median restore latency strictly below 150 seconds, and successful restores divided by attempted restores of at least 99 percent. A median of exactly 150 seconds fails. Compare the unrounded success fraction against the threshold; a display rounded to 99 percent does not prove compliance.\nThese conditions apply to the recorded nightly restore workload. They do not establish behavior during power failures.",
                "score": 6.5476680249,
                "start": 0,
                "title": "01-night-restore-rule.md",
                "source": "synthetic:harbor/01-night-restore-rule.md",
                "chunk_id": "chunk:07ce18e6409ea51aec448738",
